        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T15:29:12Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Ah if `CreateBuffer` fails and returns null because of MappedAtCreation IMHO we can crash because that\u0027s an unrecoverable OOM. Maybe adding this CHECK in `CreateBuffer` will help simplify the logic? I am very concerned about the current amount of state in that one function because it will make any future changes in the area very hard to get right (just as much as this one is hard).\n\nBasically APICreateBuffer is impossible to make sense of at the moment because 5 different code paths are merged together and not contiguous so I\u0027m trying to find solutions to untangle things a bit.",
      "parentUuid": "a9dee998_c7f31f6d",
      "revId": "7f15bb39b2b8036bea670db741efe151a93f80bf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79ad6c10_9689e70a",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 1978,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-18T03:10:57Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a good idea to just crash if mappedAtCreation OOM happens internally, it should propagate out to a device loss. `AllowedErrorTests.QueueCopyTextureForBrowserOomBuffer` actually tests this for one internal use.\n\nI don\u0027t think the layering of the CreateBuffer calls themselves can be reduced.\n- APICreateBuffer should return a valid buffer, ErrorBuffer, or null, depending on the circumstance.\n- CreateBuffer should return an ErrorData on any type of error (including both mappedAtCreation-OOM and device-OOM).\n\nSo:\n- APICreateBuffer-\u003eCreateBuffer doesn\u0027t work because then we have to unpack the ErrorData to figure out what to do.\n- CreateBuffer-\u003eAPICreateBuffer doesn\u0027t work because we\u0027ve lost the ErrorData already. We can\u0027t make a new one because we don\u0027t know the type.\n\nHowever I can try to simplify the layering of MapAtCreation by having one function that returns something like `std::variant\u003cvalid buffer, map oom ErrorData, other ErrorData\u003e` (and does the mapping) and then CreateBuffer and APICreateBuffer just call that and decide what to do with it. TBD.",
      "parentUuid": "300c0de4_bb232c85",
      "revId": "7f15bb39b2b8036bea670db741efe151a93f80bf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "028cfd5e_fdf87e0c",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
