      "writtenOn": "2025-03-18T13:12:47Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a good idea to just crash if mappedAtCreation OOM happens internally, it should propagate out to a device loss.\n\nThat could be handled in `CreateBuffer` no? Detect that there is a nullptr and decide that it was a mappedAtCreation failure. My suggestion is to have both `CreateBuffer` and `APICreateBuffer` call `ResultOrError\u003c(Nullable)Ref\u003cBuffer\u003e\u003e CreateBufferInternal(UnpackedDesc)` and decide what to do in the various cases.",
      "parentUuid": "79ad6c10_9689e70a",
      "revId": "7f15bb39b2b8036bea670db741efe151a93f80bf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
